{%- comment -%}
  Free-shipping progress bar for the cart drawer.

  A labelled progress bar showing how close the cart is to free shipping,
  counted in BOXES (not £) so a discount code can never pull the cart back
  under the threshold. Two states: a goal prompt ("buy two boxes" / "buy
  another box" once one is in, partial fill) and "unlocked" (full fill +
  success message), pluralised on boxes-needed.

  Qualified = ANY line is a subscription (it carries a selling plan, from
  ReCharge or Loop alike — subscribers get free shipping regardless of what is
  in the cart) OR the cart subtotal reaches the minimum spend. One-off carts
  below it keep the progress prompt. Mirrors the two automatic free-shipping
  discounts in Shopify admin (purchase type Subscription; minimum purchase
  amount). Pure Liquid — it reads cart.items_subtotal_price and is re-rendered
  on every cart change because it lives inside the drawer's [data-drawer-body],
  which cart-drawer.js swaps via the Section Rendering API. No client JS.

  Measured in £, not items: the custom box is sold as individual packs (one cart
  line per flavour), so counting items would count packs, not boxes. A box is
  six packs at £3 or a pre-made six-pack at £18, so "two boxes" = the minimum
  spend; the "boxes still needed" copy is that shortfall in box-prices.

  IMPORTANT: Shopify does not expose an automatic discount's threshold to Liquid
  (free-shipping discounts are shipping-level, applied at checkout). So
  `threshold` must be mirrored here from the discount config — the two can drift
  if only one is changed. The matching discount rule is "minimum purchase amount"
  = the same number.

  Owned by sections/cart-drawer.liquid.

  Expects:
    - threshold: minimum spend that unlocks free shipping, in the store
      currency's major unit (e.g. 36). Bar is hidden when blank or <= 0.
    - box_price: price of one box in the same unit (e.g. 18), used only for the
      "buy another box" wording.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cart-shipping-progress', threshold: section.settings.free_shipping_min_spend, box_price: section.settings.free_shipping_box_price %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign threshold_cents = threshold | times: 100 | round
  assign box_cents = box_price | times: 100 | round
  if box_cents < 1
    assign box_cents = threshold_cents
  endif
  assign subtotal_cents = cart.items_subtotal_price

  assign has_subscription = false
  for item in cart.items
    if item.selling_plan_allocation != blank
      assign has_subscription = true
      break
    endif
  endfor

  assign qualified = false
  if has_subscription
    assign qualified = true
  elsif threshold_cents > 0 and subtotal_cents >= threshold_cents
    assign qualified = true
  endif

  # Boxes still needed for the "buy another box" / "buy two boxes" copy.
  # Always >= 1 in the unqualified branch.
  assign remaining_cents = threshold_cents | minus: subtotal_cents
  assign boxes_needed = remaining_cents | divided_by: box_cents | ceil
  if boxes_needed < 1
    assign boxes_needed = 1
  endif

  assign percent = 0
  if qualified
    assign percent = 100
  elsif threshold_cents > 0
    assign percent = subtotal_cents | times: 100.00 | divided_by: threshold_cents
    if percent > 100
      assign percent = 100
    endif
  endif
  assign percent_aria = percent | round
-%}

{%- if threshold_cents > 0 -%}
  <div class="cart-shipping-progress{% if qualified %} is-qualified{% endif %}">
    <p class="cart-shipping-progress-message text-ui">
      {%- if qualified -%}
        {{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_qualified' | t }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_remaining' | t: count: boxes_needed }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
    <div
      class="cart-shipping-progress-track"
      role="progressbar"
      aria-valuemin="0"
      aria-valuemax="100"
      aria-valuenow="{{ percent_aria }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'cart.drawer.shipping_progress_label' | t }}"
    >
      <div class="cart-shipping-progress-fill" style="--fill: {{ percent }}%;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .cart-shipping-progress {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--spacing-xxs);
    padding: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress-message {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress.is-qualified .cart-shipping-progress-message {
    color: #479d28;
  }

  .cart-shipping-progress-track {
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: var(--rad-s);
    background: var(--color-border);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Width animates via transition (not @keyframes) so a cart update slides the
     fill from its current position to the new target. cart-drawer.js carries
     the outgoing width onto the freshly-swapped element to make that work — a
     bare transition alone can't, because the body innerHTML swap mounts a new
     fill node each refresh. */
  .cart-shipping-progress-fill {
    height: 100%;
    width: var(--fill);
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    transition: width var(--transition-slow);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .cart-shipping-progress-fill {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
